CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS AND AUTHORITIES OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 5
(1) In providing protection to victims of gender-based and child violence, the Regional Government has the obligation to:
a. implement all efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence;
b. provide protection for victims of violence;
c. provide recovery services and social reintegration for victims;
d. encourage and increase community participation;
e. cooperate with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence; and
f. supervise the implementation of services for victims involving the community.
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based and child violence;
b. facilitate the implementation of integrated services;
c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. conduct coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based and child violence; and
f. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The regional government in carrying out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

Article 14
Community participation as referred to in Article 8 letter e is carried out through:
a. providing protection for victims;
b. providing emergency assistance;
c. providing advocacy to victims and/or the community regarding the handling of cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. assisting in the process of submitting applications for the determination of protection;
e. conveying information to the competent authorities related to cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
f. fostering local wisdom in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
g. organizing the strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and violence against children; and
h. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and violence against children;

CHAPTER II
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 4
(1) Every victim of gender-based violence and child victim of violence has the right to:
    a. obtain protection for personal security, family and property, and freedom from threats related to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given;
    b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
    c. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
    d. obtain integrated services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and in accordance with needs;
    e. recovery and social reintegration;
    f. obtain legal assistance, psychological, spiritual guidance, economic, social and interpreter services;
    g. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
    h. obtain guarantees of their rights related to their status as wife/mother, husband/father, child and household member as well as community member; and
    i. obtain information about laws and regulations that protect victims.
(2) The Rights of Victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF DEMAK,
Considering:
a. that all forms of violence, especially gender-based violence and violence against children are violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity as well as forms of discrimination;
b. that victims of gender-based violence and violence against children must receive protection, both from the regional government and/or the community in order to avoid and be free from violence and/or threats of violence within the scope of the household and community;
c. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community are obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Violence Against Children;
